## Key OPSEC Failures

| Mistake | Impact |
|---|---|
| Used real surname fragment in ProtonMail address (`martinez`) | Linked anonymous forum post to real identity |
| Posted contact email publicly on criminal forum | Trivial cross-platform attribution |
| Same "Phoenix" motif across all aliases, company name, and street address | Made pivot chain obvious |
| Registered a legitimate company under real name for an illicit business | Full legal identity exposed via public business registry |
| SSH config pasted verbatim in tech support post | Leaked infrastructure key identifier |

